% A chemistry lab computes the molar mass of six compounds from the standard
% atomic weights of their elements, kept exact as whole milligrams per mole.
% It concludes, for example, that water has a molar mass of 18015 mg/mol and
% glucose 180156 mg/mol, that oxygen makes up 888 per mille of the mass of
% water, that glucose is the heaviest of the six and that methane and ammonia
% each weigh less than water.
% Shows a sum over a formula's parts with a product in its condition, integer
% division for per mille shares, a maximum and a comparison of computed values.
% Atomic weights after the IUPAC standard atomic weights, abridged to five
% significant figures.

the templates are:
    *an element* has an atomic weight of *a number* mg per mole,
    *a compound* has *a number* atoms of *an element*,
    the molar mass of *a compound* is *a number* mg per mole,
    *an element* makes up *a number* per mille of *a compound*,
    *a compound* is lighter than *a compound*,
    the heaviest compound weighs *a number* mg per mole,
    *a compound* is the heaviest compound.

the knowledge base chemistry includes:

% A compound weighs the sum of its atoms: each element's count times its
% atomic weight.
the molar mass of a compound is a mass mg per mole
    if the compound has a number atoms of an element
    and the mass is the sum of each part such that
        the compound has a number N atoms of an element E
        and E has an atomic weight of a number W mg per mole
        and the part = N * W.

% An element's share of a compound's mass, in whole per mille, rounded down.
an element makes up a share per mille of a compound
    if the compound has a number N atoms of the element
    and the element has an atomic weight of a number W mg per mole
    and the molar mass of the compound is a mass mg per mole
    and the share = 1000 * N * W // the mass.

a compound is lighter than an other compound
    if the molar mass of the compound is a first mass mg per mole
    and the molar mass of the other compound is a second mass mg per mole
    and the first mass < the second mass.

the heaviest compound weighs a mass mg per mole
    if the mass is the max of each M such that
        the molar mass of a compound is M mg per mole.

a compound is the heaviest compound
    if the heaviest compound weighs a mass mg per mole
    and the molar mass of the compound is the mass mg per mole.

scenario lab is:
    hydrogen has an atomic weight of 1008 mg per mole.
    carbon has an atomic weight of 12011 mg per mole.
    nitrogen has an atomic weight of 14007 mg per mole.
    oxygen has an atomic weight of 15999 mg per mole.
    sodium has an atomic weight of 22990 mg per mole.
    chlorine has an atomic weight of 35453 mg per mole.
    water has 2 atoms of hydrogen.
    water has 1 atoms of oxygen.
    carbon dioxide has 1 atoms of carbon.
    carbon dioxide has 2 atoms of oxygen.
    methane has 1 atoms of carbon.
    methane has 4 atoms of hydrogen.
    ammonia has 1 atoms of nitrogen.
    ammonia has 3 atoms of hydrogen.
    sodium chloride has 1 atoms of sodium.
    sodium chloride has 1 atoms of chlorine.
    glucose has 6 atoms of carbon.
    glucose has 12 atoms of hydrogen.
    glucose has 6 atoms of oxygen.
    masses expects answers ["the molar mass of water is 18015 mg per mole",
        "the molar mass of carbon dioxide is 44009 mg per mole",
        "the molar mass of methane is 16043 mg per mole",
        "the molar mass of ammonia is 17031 mg per mole",
        "the molar mass of sodium chloride is 58443 mg per mole",
        "the molar mass of glucose is 180156 mg per mole"].
    oxygen expects answers ["oxygen makes up 888 per mille of water", "oxygen makes up 727 per mille of carbon dioxide",
        "oxygen makes up 532 per mille of glucose"].
    heaviest expects answers ["glucose is the heaviest compound"].
    lighter expects answers ["methane is lighter than water", "ammonia is lighter than water"].

query masses is:
    the molar mass of which compound is which number mg per mole.

query oxygen is:
    oxygen makes up which share per mille of which compound.

query heaviest is:
    which compound is the heaviest compound.

query lighter is:
    which compound is lighter than water.
